WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.390
If you want to hear my theory about what the
heck is going on here -- why is this is Jack-o-lantern

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:11.809
in the fishtank? -- then stick around to the
end of this video.

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:14.010
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.980
Earlier this week we talked about the trailer
for the new Halloween movie.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.920
If you haven't seen that video click on over
here to check it out.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.570
And in the comments for that video you guys
had some excellent points that I didn't touch

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.109
on in the first video.

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:29.369
In the original Halloween , the first guy
Michael kills in 1978 is this mechanic from

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:30.369
Phelps Garage.

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:34.089
Dr. Loomis finds the hospital gown in the
bushes and we pull out to see the guy has

00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:37.390
been killed, his corpse is in the bushes and
his clothes have been taken.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.699
So that's how Michael got his iconic garb.

00:00:39.699 --> 00:00:42.969
Facestabber51 brought this up in the comments
and it made me realize something about the

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:46.309
new trailer, where we see this scene taking
place at an auto service center.

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:49.300
The British guy goes in and finds a body in
a puddle of blood.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.860
He appears to be the mechanic and he's in
his underwear.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.579
Not only is this paying tribute to John Carpenter's
Halloween, but it tells us that Michael seems

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:58.609
to be retracing his steps from all those years
ago.

00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:02.559
That brings me to another comment, which theorizes
that Michael's rampage in old Halloween, was

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:07.210
never about going after Laurie, but rather
reliving the night he killed his sister Judith.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.850
And I agree and disagree with this.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.890
He does seem to be targeting Laurie, ever
since he sees her drop off that key at the

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.420
Myers house for her father, who is a realtor
who is trying to sell the house, but he can't

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.500
because everyone in town thinks it's haunted.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.369
And let's face it, it kind of looks like ****.

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:23.150
Because from that point, he's watching her
in school, following her around town, and

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.590
turning up at the house she babysits that
night.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:29.390
The part I do agree with, which is a great
point, is the idea that Michael tries to recreate

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:32.299
the circumstances of Judith's murder when
he kills Annie.

00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:36.399
Both start with seeing the victim undressed
from outside, he kills both with the knife

00:01:36.399 --> 00:01:40.920
and then moves Annie to the bed under Judith's
tombstone to complete his recreation.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:47.330
So my point is, if 1978 was Michael Myers's
recreation of 1963, then maybe 2018 is a recreation

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:51.539
of 1978, starting with him killing a mechanic
for his clothes, stealing the mask, doing

00:01:51.539 --> 00:01:56.000
the ghost sheet thing, and this time, trying
not to let Laurie Strode get away.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.170
We don't know how Michael gets his mask back
in this movie, or even if it is the very same

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:03.369
mask at all, but a couple of you theorized
that he gets his old mask from this guy.

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:08.020
Some of you think he's the new head psychiatrist
at Smith's Grove, some say he's even related

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.120
to Dr. Loomis while others see say he's just
a documentarian.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.950
But many of you noticed if you pause right
here, it's actually his head being bashed

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.400
into the bathroom stall door.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.460
So Michael probably takes him out to steal
back the mask.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:22.980
And maybe this location is Phelps Garage, which is only referenced on this side of this truck in the first one.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.120
In the last video I said that the bathroom
scene was a callback to H20 where the woman

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.660
gets attacked, but Joshua Wilson brings up
a good point, he never actually attacked her,

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.830
he just scared her and stole her car.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:38.819
Someone else brought up another possible H20
reference, that being a waist high shot of

00:02:38.819 --> 00:02:40.720
Michael doing this little knife flip move.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.681
I'm not sure if that's exclusive to H20 and
I'm not about to rewatch them all to find

00:02:44.681 --> 00:02:45.681
out.

00:02:45.681 --> 00:02:46.730
I'll just take your word for it, it's a nice
little find..

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:50.760
OK, I love this next one, suggested by Lowbudget
Skitz.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.650
In the clip where Laurie yells at the trick-or-treaters
to get inside there's a quick glimpse of two

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:59.780
kids running away wearing Silver Shamrock
masks from Halloween 3: Season of the Witch.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.799
If you haven't seen it, the masks are a major
plot-point of Halloween 3, so this is a really

00:03:03.799 --> 00:03:05.760
cool split-second reference.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.210
Moving on, I had previously said I thought
this photo could be Tommy Doyle and many of

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.360
you said you thought it was young Michael
Myers.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.989
Those of you who said that were correct, and
here's why.

00:03:13.989 --> 00:03:17.860
This file is probably Michael's file at Smith's
Grove where he was a patient starting at age

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:18.860
6.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:21.239
This white wall looks like something out of
the sanitarium, not a house.

00:03:21.239 --> 00:03:24.420
The kid in the photo has shorts on, which
Tommy does not at the end of Halloween.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.420
Michael is initially taken in wearing this
clown costume so there's a good chance he

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.930
had shorts underneath.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.120
Another correction you guys made was on this
diagram.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.841
For some reason I read this as one slash across
the neck and one across the shoulder, but

00:03:35.841 --> 00:03:40.319
looking at it again it’s clearly one slash
that stretches the neck and shoulder.

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:43.472
Plus I looked back and Laurie never actually
gets a cut on her neck, so this is an injury

00:03:43.472 --> 00:03:45.470
report on Annie, not Laurie.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:48.709
Annie gets strangled and gets her throat slit
in the car when she’s about to go pick up

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:52.650
her boyfriend, and we can see the result of
her injuries later after Michael relocates

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.760
her to the bed.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.560
John Archangel wants to know Do you think
Laurie finally got with Ben Tramer?

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:00.769
And if you don’t remember, Ben Tramer is
the guy Laurie has a crush on who’s mentioned

00:04:00.769 --> 00:04:13.219
but not seen in the first movie, and killed
off early in Halloween II....

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:18.130
BUT Halloween II doesn’t exist in this continuity,
so there’s a chance they got together.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:21.160
And Laurie does have grandkids now so you
never know.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.530
I mean, I hope for her sake that it works
out for Laurie and Ben in this continuity

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.470
because they just haven’t had any luck in
any of the others, plus it would be a cool

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:32.060
throwaway line if someone mentioned that her
husband’s name was Ben or something like

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:33.060
that.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.410
The most mysterious part of the trailer is
this Jack-o-lantern inside the fish tank.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:40.280
I don’t think it’s just a Halloween decoration
for the fishes, I actually have a theory on

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.280
it.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.660
I think this guy in the foreground, is actually
this guy, the cop.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.280
So he’s coming to this house to investigate
a disturbance.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.970
The chair’s been tipped over and there’s
blood on the floor.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.480
This sheet ghost isn’t moving.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:54.060
Either it’s Michael Myers hiding underneath
or a victim’s body that’s been covered

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.060
up.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.790
Whatever the case may be, I think someone
tried to throw the pumpkin at Michael in self

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.730
defense, missed and it just ended up landing
in the fish tank.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:01.790
But what do you think?

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:02.830
Do you think this is Michael?

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:04.180
Do you think it’s one of the victims?

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:07.440
Do you think this guy at the end of the trailer
is the real Michael, or just someone playing

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.440
a prank?

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.440
Let me know in the comments.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:12.590
And if you’ve been enjoying all the new
videos lately, let me know my giving this

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:13.590
one a like.

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:16.390
There’s a lot more to talk about so let’s
keep the discussion going.

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:20.920
Make sure you’re subscribed to CZsWorld
for new horrors every week, ring that deathbell

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:24.380
for notifications and I’ll see you in the
next one.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.880
Assuming we both survive.

